    "methods_description": "Participants performed a visual oddball P300 paradigm with target ('OOO') and non-target ('XXX') stimuli (target ratio 0.2) while walking on a treadmill at 1.6 m/s. EEG was recorded from 46 scalp channels (standard 10-20 montage) plus 14 ear-EEG channels (7 per ear), 4 EOG channels, and 6 IMU channels (3-axis accelerometer and gyroscope) at 100 Hz sampling rate. Data were epoched from -190 ms to +800 ms around stimulus onset. The dataset was originally collected as part of BCI Competition 2020 Track 5.",
